1
00:00:16,534 --> 00:00:22,869
(Firefly Theater)

2
00:00:43,456 --> 00:00:47,392
♪Neon lights twist into a knot♪

3
00:00:49,024 --> 00:00:52,608
♪I rest in the ruins of defeat♪

4
00:00:53,184 --> 00:00:55,520
♪You tap your fingers lightly♪

5
00:00:55,904 --> 00:00:58,656
♪I fall into the abyss♪

6
00:00:59,488 --> 00:01:02,080
♪I've seen this game before♪

7
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:04,768
♪Every single move was calculated♪

8
00:01:04,768 --> 00:01:07,168
♪I finally see your silhouette♪

9
00:01:07,552 --> 00:01:10,304
♪Just an empty shell♪

10
00:01:10,624 --> 00:01:13,440
♪I've broken this game before♪

11
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:15,872
♪Every move was placed wrong♪

12
00:01:15,872 --> 00:01:18,016
♪Now it's my turn to play♪

13
00:01:18,208 --> 00:01:25,056
♪I'll show you what stunning looks like♪

14
00:01:25,728 --> 00:01:28,256
♪When I stand back up again♪

15
00:01:28,544 --> 00:01:30,400
♪The whole city goes dark♪

16
00:01:31,264 --> 00:01:33,952
♪For the part you owe me♪

17
00:01:34,112 --> 00:01:41,088
♪I'll make you pay double♪

18
00:01:42,624 --> 00:01:47,360
♪You're just my starting point♪

19
00:01:51,712 --> 00:01:52,739
=The Vanishing Beauty=

20
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,720
=Episode 23=

21
00:01:56,985 --> 00:02:00,097
(Bunny Blan's Botanical Garden)

22
00:02:00,884 --> 00:02:01,565
(Wait, is there)

23
00:02:01,565 --> 00:02:02,405
(a cup missing?)

24
00:02:02,685 --> 00:02:03,484
(How much was it?)

25
00:02:04,005 --> 00:02:04,884
(I'll pay you triple.)

26
00:02:07,964 --> 00:02:08,365
Hello.

27
00:02:09,125 --> 00:02:10,245
I'm looking for a tea set

28
00:02:10,245 --> 00:02:11,245
as a gift for a woman.

29
00:02:11,604 --> 00:02:12,204
Anything

30
00:02:12,204 --> 00:02:13,285
with a stronger design?

31
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:14,764
Any recommendations?

32
00:02:15,085 --> 00:02:15,965
Sure, just a moment.

33
00:02:17,531 --> 00:02:20,468
(Di Liren)

34
00:02:23,456 --> 00:02:26,418
(Trust Company)

35
00:02:27,005 --> 00:02:27,644
Hello?

36
00:02:28,405 --> 00:02:29,245
Hello, Ms. Lu.

37
00:02:29,685 --> 00:02:30,444
Your trust account

38
00:02:30,444 --> 00:02:31,484
with us

39
00:02:31,644 --> 00:02:33,204
has had its beneficiary updated.

40
00:02:33,845 --> 00:02:35,245
It changed from Fang Haoyu

41
00:02:35,324 --> 00:02:36,204
to Yu Meng.

42
00:02:36,285 --> 00:02:36,805
Impossible.

43
00:02:36,845 --> 00:02:37,845
Did you get it wrong?

44
00:02:38,685 --> 00:02:39,405
I never changed

45
00:02:39,444 --> 00:02:40,085
the beneficiary.

46
00:02:41,164 --> 00:02:41,767
Please hold on.

47
00:02:42,604 --> 00:02:43,604
The system shows

48
00:02:43,724 --> 00:02:44,924
Fang Haoyu did it in person.

49
00:02:45,005 --> 00:02:46,604
Under the trust terms,

50
00:02:46,764 --> 00:02:47,565
the beneficiary

51
00:02:47,565 --> 00:02:48,245
can transfer it.

52
00:02:48,365 --> 00:02:49,005
That's insane.

53
00:02:50,724 --> 00:02:51,685
I set up the trust.

54
00:02:51,924 --> 00:02:53,365
It requires my signed authorization.

55
00:02:54,685 --> 00:02:55,365
You must revoke

56
00:02:55,525 --> 00:02:56,525
the transfer immediately.

57
00:02:57,125 --> 00:02:58,644
I'm sorry. We can't do that.

58
00:02:59,204 --> 00:03:00,444
Once the trust takes effect,

59
00:03:00,565 --> 00:03:02,405
disposition rights
belong to the beneficiary.

60
00:03:17,324 --> 00:03:18,511
Where's the trust I gave you?

61
00:03:19,724 --> 00:03:20,444
I gave it to Meng

62
00:03:20,764 --> 00:03:21,546
as a birthday gift.

63
00:03:23,365 --> 00:03:24,186
Why give it to her?

64
00:03:25,085 --> 00:03:26,085
Did you even ask me?

65
00:03:26,644 --> 00:03:27,724
Did you ask for my opinion

66
00:03:27,764 --> 00:03:29,044
when you sent me abroad?

67
00:03:29,965 --> 00:03:30,444
That money

68
00:03:30,444 --> 00:03:31,164
was always Meng's.

69
00:03:31,204 --> 00:03:31,884
I didn't give it.

70
00:03:32,125 --> 00:03:32,725
I returned it.

71
00:03:33,565 --> 00:03:34,005
Did...

72
00:03:34,724 --> 00:03:36,017
Did someone feed you nonsense?

73
00:03:36,324 --> 00:03:36,965
Including what

74
00:03:36,965 --> 00:03:37,644
you and Dad said?

75
00:03:39,125 --> 00:03:39,724
I heard

76
00:03:40,324 --> 00:03:41,484
everything at the restaurant.

77
00:03:41,884 --> 00:03:42,805
Dad took all that money

78
00:03:42,884 --> 00:03:43,884
from the Yu family.

79
00:03:44,845 --> 00:03:45,164
Mom,

80
00:03:46,285 --> 00:03:47,044
you knew that money

81
00:03:47,044 --> 00:03:47,644
was dirty.

82
00:03:48,085 --> 00:03:49,125
Why did you still keep it?

83
00:03:51,484 --> 00:03:52,484
To secure your future.

84
00:03:53,565 --> 00:03:54,405
With that money,

85
00:03:55,525 --> 00:03:57,164
you wouldn't worry about surgery costs,

86
00:03:58,204 --> 00:03:59,484
and you'd be set for life.

87
00:04:01,044 --> 00:04:01,685
I couldn't bear

88
00:04:01,764 --> 00:04:03,005
to watch my child suffer again,

89
00:04:03,285 --> 00:04:04,232
too poor for treatment.

90
00:04:04,484 --> 00:04:05,365
But I can work.

91
00:04:05,484 --> 00:04:06,565
I can support myself.

92
00:04:06,644 --> 00:04:07,044
I solve

93
00:04:07,085 --> 00:04:07,924
my own problems.

94
00:04:08,005 --> 00:04:08,845
I'm not helpless.

95
00:04:10,085 --> 00:04:10,685
Even if...

96
00:04:11,285 --> 00:04:12,245
Even if I drop school

97
00:04:12,444 --> 00:04:13,204
or have to starve,

98
00:04:13,324 --> 00:04:14,005
I will pay back

99
00:04:14,044 --> 00:04:14,644
the money.

100
00:04:15,565 --> 00:04:17,125
You're so naive.

101
00:04:18,284 --> 00:04:19,365
Money's not easy to make.

102
00:04:19,565 --> 00:04:20,324
Without a degree,

103
00:04:20,444 --> 00:04:21,460
what job could you get?

104
00:04:21,605 --> 00:04:22,485
How will you repay it?

105
00:04:22,485 --> 00:04:23,125
With what?

106
00:04:25,884 --> 00:04:26,565
Listen to me,

107
00:04:27,925 --> 00:04:29,844
let's go to the trust company right now,

108
00:04:30,764 --> 00:04:31,964
revoke the transfer,

109
00:04:32,324 --> 00:04:33,365
and get the money back,

110
00:04:33,365 --> 00:04:33,884
okay?

111
00:04:34,524 --> 00:04:35,485
Dad said the same thing.

112
00:04:37,284 --> 00:04:38,125
But his reaction

113
00:04:39,964 --> 00:04:40,565
was far worse.

114
00:04:41,204 --> 00:04:42,045
You told your dad

115
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:44,444
you gave the trust away?

116
00:04:45,444 --> 00:04:46,725
He'd find out sooner or later.

117
00:04:47,764 --> 00:04:48,964
I wanted him to know

118
00:04:49,005 --> 00:04:49,524
my resolve.

119
00:04:57,444 --> 00:04:57,925
Mom,

120
00:05:00,644 --> 00:05:01,245
I know

121
00:05:01,605 --> 00:05:02,524
how much you and Dad

122
00:05:02,605 --> 00:05:03,725
have sacrificed for me.

123
00:05:04,524 --> 00:05:05,125
And I know

124
00:05:05,844 --> 00:05:06,485
without you two,

125
00:05:07,284 --> 00:05:08,005
I wouldn't have

126
00:05:08,005 --> 00:05:08,764
such a good life.

127
00:05:09,245 --> 00:05:10,245
But I can't just stand by

128
00:05:10,245 --> 00:05:11,045
and let you do wrong

129
00:05:11,125 --> 00:05:12,005
just for my sake.

130
00:05:13,125 --> 00:05:13,725
All I want

131
00:05:14,284 --> 00:05:15,805
is for you, Dad,

132
00:05:16,045 --> 00:05:16,925
and me

133
00:05:17,245 --> 00:05:17,685
to live

134
00:05:17,764 --> 00:05:19,125
safe and sound together.

135
00:05:20,005 --> 00:05:20,764
Let's just

136
00:05:21,045 --> 00:05:21,805
drop the trust.

137
00:05:21,844 --> 00:05:22,764
Just let it go.

138
00:05:24,204 --> 00:05:24,685
Okay?

139
00:05:25,204 --> 00:05:26,579
You've never faced the real world.

140
00:05:29,404 --> 00:05:30,605
You don't know what the money

141
00:05:32,084 --> 00:05:33,125
means for you.

142
00:05:33,964 --> 00:05:34,964
When you're older,

143
00:05:35,884 --> 00:05:37,084
you'll understand.

144
00:05:38,045 --> 00:05:39,045
When you were little

145
00:05:39,125 --> 00:05:39,844
and wouldn't eat,

146
00:05:42,045 --> 00:05:43,005
I had to chase after you

147
00:05:43,125 --> 00:05:44,764
to feed you bite by bite.

148
00:05:46,324 --> 00:05:47,165
I know what's

149
00:05:47,165 --> 00:05:47,884
best for you.

150
00:05:49,245 --> 00:05:50,644
I can't let this money go.

151
00:05:52,245 --> 00:05:52,605
Mom.

152
00:05:53,485 --> 00:05:53,884
Mom!

153
00:06:02,964 --> 00:06:03,884
You liar!

154
00:06:04,964 --> 00:06:05,524
You promised

155
00:06:05,605 --> 00:06:06,524
to cut ties with Haoyu.

156
00:06:06,964 --> 00:06:07,925
You broke your word

157
00:06:08,644 --> 00:06:09,204
and even went

158
00:06:09,245 --> 00:06:10,204
after his trust fund.

159
00:06:10,764 --> 00:06:11,365
You tricked him

160
00:06:11,404 --> 00:06:12,332
into giving it to you,

161
00:06:12,644 --> 00:06:13,084
didn't you?

162
00:06:14,964 --> 00:06:15,752
You misunderstood.

163
00:06:16,404 --> 00:06:17,284
The trust caught me

164
00:06:18,245 --> 00:06:18,964
by surprise too.

165
00:06:19,245 --> 00:06:20,685
Then give it back to Haoyu.

166
00:06:22,725 --> 00:06:23,404
Impossible.

167
00:06:24,084 --> 00:06:24,925
That money was ours

168
00:06:24,964 --> 00:06:25,617
to begin with.

169
00:06:25,805 --> 00:06:27,241
Di Liren earned every cent of it.

170
00:06:27,884 --> 00:06:29,125
He worked his heart out

171
00:06:29,485 --> 00:06:30,404
to build up Jiali.

172
00:06:30,764 --> 00:06:31,884
That's what he deserved.

173
00:06:33,245 --> 00:06:34,245
He was willing

174
00:06:34,404 --> 00:06:35,485
to stay and work at Jiali

175
00:06:36,204 --> 00:06:37,284
only to secure a safety net

176
00:06:37,524 --> 00:06:38,805
and a future for Haoyu.

177
00:06:39,045 --> 00:06:39,644
That money

178
00:06:40,005 --> 00:06:41,045
should go to Haoyu.

179
00:06:41,524 --> 00:06:43,165
Without the platform my family provided

180
00:06:43,524 --> 00:06:44,565
and all those connections,

181
00:06:44,805 --> 00:06:45,644
could he make it?

182
00:06:46,005 --> 00:06:46,884
He couldn't even get

183
00:06:46,925 --> 00:06:47,590
into the circle.

184
00:06:48,284 --> 00:06:48,925
I understand

185
00:06:48,964 --> 00:06:50,084
your feelings as a mother.

186
00:06:51,284 --> 00:06:52,725
But let me ask you,

187
00:06:53,524 --> 00:06:54,644
do you really know Harry?

188
00:06:55,284 --> 00:06:55,764
He's

189
00:06:55,764 --> 00:06:57,084
an independent, grown adult.

190
00:06:57,245 --> 00:06:58,565
He's capable and talented.

191
00:06:58,764 --> 00:06:59,524
He can already

192
00:06:59,524 --> 00:07:01,045
make a living with his own hands.

193
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:02,844
Look around here.

194
00:07:03,764 --> 00:07:04,805
Every single detail here

195
00:07:05,844 --> 00:07:06,365
was designed

196
00:07:06,365 --> 00:07:07,324
by Harry personally.

197
00:07:11,685 --> 00:07:13,125
Look at these simple-looking lights.

198
00:07:14,005 --> 00:07:15,045
He calculated

199
00:07:15,485 --> 00:07:16,485
each one's angle

200
00:07:16,925 --> 00:07:17,764
so the light

201
00:07:17,884 --> 00:07:19,245
would shine without glaring

202
00:07:19,444 --> 00:07:20,805
into the customers' eyes.

203
00:07:22,245 --> 00:07:23,165
And these chairs.

204
00:07:24,005 --> 00:07:24,725
He visited

205
00:07:24,844 --> 00:07:26,045
every furniture market,

206
00:07:26,204 --> 00:07:27,404
testing out each chair himself

207
00:07:27,524 --> 00:07:28,352
before picking them.

208
00:07:28,725 --> 00:07:30,125
He said a backrest with this curve

209
00:07:30,404 --> 00:07:31,324
is ergonomic,

210
00:07:31,725 --> 00:07:32,925
so customers won't get tired.

211
00:07:33,805 --> 00:07:34,764
He went through

212
00:07:34,805 --> 00:07:35,964
eight whole drafts

213
00:07:36,045 --> 00:07:37,565
for the color palette of

214
00:07:37,644 --> 00:07:38,045
the space,

215
00:07:38,204 --> 00:07:38,925
walls, carpets,

216
00:07:38,964 --> 00:07:39,644
and furniture.

217
00:07:39,844 --> 00:07:40,964
He even mixed the wall paint

218
00:07:41,084 --> 00:07:41,925
a dozen times to get

219
00:07:42,005 --> 00:07:42,764
the shade right.

220
00:07:43,485 --> 00:07:44,284
Every customer

221
00:07:44,485 --> 00:07:45,644
who walks in praises it.

222
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:47,844
For a place this big,

223
00:07:48,884 --> 00:07:49,764
with so many floors,

224
00:07:51,565 --> 00:07:52,844
he must have worn himself out.

225
00:07:54,084 --> 00:07:54,844
All this is just

226
00:07:55,524 --> 00:07:56,404
to let you know

227
00:07:57,125 --> 00:07:58,284
he truly loves this work.

228
00:07:58,485 --> 00:07:59,764
And he has the eye, the taste,

229
00:07:59,764 --> 00:08:00,404
and the talent.

230
00:08:00,844 --> 00:08:01,524
But you?

231
00:08:01,805 --> 00:08:02,805
You don't support him

232
00:08:02,884 --> 00:08:03,524
or see him.

233
00:08:03,644 --> 00:08:04,644
You keep sheltering him

234
00:08:04,725 --> 00:08:05,764
in a glass dome,

235
00:08:05,884 --> 00:08:06,524
planning a life

236
00:08:06,565 --> 00:08:07,685
he doesn't want.

237
00:08:08,045 --> 00:08:09,605
Is that really good for him?

238
00:08:10,045 --> 00:08:11,204
Will he truly be happy?

239
00:08:13,964 --> 00:08:14,884
I believe one day,

240
00:08:16,444 --> 00:08:17,365
when he's older,

241
00:08:18,204 --> 00:08:18,805
he'll get it

242
00:08:19,565 --> 00:08:20,524
and come around.

243
00:08:23,324 --> 00:08:24,764
You're the one who needs to get it.

244
00:08:32,684 --> 00:08:33,164
Alright,

245
00:08:34,125 --> 00:08:35,205
considering Harry

246
00:08:36,044 --> 00:08:37,284
returned the money on his own

247
00:08:37,804 --> 00:08:38,965
and saved me a lot of hassle,

248
00:08:39,764 --> 00:08:40,644
I can give him a share

249
00:08:40,725 --> 00:08:41,605
of the benefits.

250
00:08:41,965 --> 00:08:43,884
It'll ensure he finishes his studies

251
00:08:44,044 --> 00:08:44,965
and fulfill

252
00:08:45,245 --> 00:08:46,524
your wish as a mother.

253
00:08:46,804 --> 00:08:47,564
Everyone wins.

254
00:08:48,044 --> 00:08:48,445
Okay?

255
00:08:51,245 --> 00:08:52,205
Only one option?

256
00:08:52,884 --> 00:08:53,485
What else?

257
00:08:54,044 --> 00:08:55,485
You have to give Haoyu

258
00:08:55,564 --> 00:08:56,644
half the benefits.

259
00:08:57,445 --> 00:08:57,884
Remember,

260
00:08:59,005 --> 00:08:59,924
I still have Weng Xin's

261
00:09:00,044 --> 00:09:01,044
wellness center records

262
00:09:01,044 --> 00:09:01,804
that you want.

263
00:09:02,884 --> 00:09:03,445
Ms. Hui,

264
00:09:03,965 --> 00:09:04,644
I'm done haggling

265
00:09:04,644 --> 00:09:05,485
with you.

266
00:09:06,125 --> 00:09:07,125
Ten percent

267
00:09:07,164 --> 00:09:07,884
is my final offer.

268
00:09:08,644 --> 00:09:09,644
If you don't agree,

269
00:09:10,644 --> 00:09:11,564
you'll face two issues.

270
00:09:12,284 --> 00:09:12,804
First,

271
00:09:13,485 --> 00:09:14,564
knowing Harry,

272
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:15,365
he will never

273
00:09:15,445 --> 00:09:16,325
touch this money.

274
00:09:18,764 --> 00:09:19,125
Second,

275
00:09:19,644 --> 00:09:20,684
I'll go after Di Liren

276
00:09:20,725 --> 00:09:21,924
for moving the assets,

277
00:09:22,485 --> 00:09:23,605
and Harry will inevitably

278
00:09:24,005 --> 00:09:24,884
face a lawsuit.

279
00:09:25,845 --> 00:09:26,725
That's certainly not

280
00:09:27,164 --> 00:09:27,884
the outcome

281
00:09:27,884 --> 00:09:28,804
you want to see.

282
00:09:31,644 --> 00:09:32,284
Think it over

283
00:09:32,965 --> 00:09:33,564
and answer me.

284
00:09:39,524 --> 00:09:40,284
Why is Mr. Di here?

285
00:09:40,404 --> 00:09:41,325
Did he get the notice?

286
00:09:41,365 --> 00:09:41,884
No way.

287
00:09:52,510 --> 00:09:55,643
(Chairman's Office)

288
00:09:58,965 --> 00:10:00,965
This leather chair
is really comfortable.

289
00:10:01,644 --> 00:10:03,245
And I just found out

290
00:10:03,485 --> 00:10:05,764
it reclines automatically.

291
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:08,365
Guess you really get what you pay for.

292
00:10:08,804 --> 00:10:09,524
Get up.

293
00:10:10,044 --> 00:10:11,164
Don't dirty my chair.

294
00:10:12,085 --> 00:10:12,804
We're brothers.

295
00:10:12,965 --> 00:10:14,485
Why split what's yours and mine?

296
00:10:15,164 --> 00:10:16,365
What's yours is mine.

297
00:10:16,404 --> 00:10:16,965
What's mine

298
00:10:17,725 --> 00:10:18,764
is still mine, of course.

299
00:10:19,605 --> 00:10:21,085
I said get up. Didn't you hear me?

300
